    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78386.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "What's frustrating to me, again, I'm somebody that pays us taxes, comes to work every day, takes care of my family, like a lot of our listeners, I don't fall into any of these special categories. I'm not over the age of 65. I've never been wounded in the military. And we rushed out to the polls thinking we were going to get some sort of relief. And we're not asking for a free pass here. Like just going back to 2021, which I thought was a pretty fair compromise, but the very first thing this committee did was strip it down. And when you try to get some sort of answers from people like Senator Baldwin and some of these other folks, you can't find them anywhere. Has that been frustrating for you?",
