    "turn_text": "Well, a little bit, but not unexpected because most of these folks that are fighting hard are Republicans that are running most of the local governments throughout the state. But they've got a homeowner's hat too, but they also sit on a local council, commissioners, mayor, or might be on the school board. And then they start to think, in a way to where they're defending the entity. And all I'm saying is, be honest, be fair, if you kept your tax rates rates down low to apply to that high assessed value, you're not going to feel much pain anyway. Some people would say, well, we didn't raise the tax rate. Well, that means you had a windfall. And every district Every local government jurisdiction is a little different. We'll end up with something that's better, I think, than what we've got. And we won two out of the three. We made it transparent. We've capped it in a way that'll be reasonable going forward. Even with their version, we might try to tweak that. We got to find more real relief for a broader spectrum of taxpayers. And I'm going to be out there making the case.",
