    "turn_idx": 35,
    "turn_text": "So we've got 92 counties and everyone is a different version. Hamilton County is a rare county. They're gonna figure it out one way or the other. They got a broad tax base. They'd be ones that like to spend through their local school districts and governments and maybe most of them are okay with it, probably not some on each end again. Then you've got some rural counties that have been losing population, their tax bases haven't been expanding, like Boone County. It's been in the Catbird seat. My county does well. But there are at least 70 to 75 counties that are struggling because that isn't going up. And that's where the tax bills have really gone up in a way that we need to be cognizant of. And those are the folks I'm going to be looking to help. And I think we'll still get there.",
