    "turn_idx": 39,
    "turn_text": "So the irony of it is with nearly every one of them prior to when that was going to go into the committee hearing and take the vote. So they know the case from my point of view. They know where maybe leadership was wanting to go and they've had an earful from all the folks that might have a vested interest whether it's just to protect their domain and like anything even if you're a conservative I've seen him left and right coming out the DC with their big old Stetson there wanting more money dumped into it right I'd say get a new business partner the federal government's going broke they'd agree with me And it wouldn't take him more than 30 seconds to say, well, can you bump my budget for next year, five to 10%? That is just part of it. And it happens across government. Here, I've been on record. Local government and school districts have to be healthy. But there's a point where they got to get efficiencies worked into it. And then I'll point out, did you take advantage of the windfall because you could? And that's where we'll end up. And that's how we'll get it figured out.",
